1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
How to download and import animation from Mixamo?

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:07,000
How to download animation from Mixamo and import it into the software?

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,000
We will export and upload the customized virtual model to Mixamo.

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:14,000
After the upload and binding is done, we need to download the model of T-Pose first.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:18,000
After downloading the model of T-Pose, we can choose the animation we need,

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,000
then select the settings we need to download the animation file.

7
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Import the FBX file into Marvelous Designer,

8
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:29,000
click the bottom triangle and check the key animation in the animation editor to see if it is correctly imported.

9
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:34,000
All videos are imported with the following options.

10
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Now we choose the animation value of this animation,

11
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:44,000
and it will appear in the Motion folder.

12
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Finally, we create a new project,

13
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:48,000
import the T-Pose virtual model that was downloaded before,

14
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:50,000
and then import the saved animation.

15
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:53,000
When importing, click to move to the beginning,

16
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:55,000
and click to switch to the first motion.

17
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Now the T-Pose moved to the beginning of the animation will automatically appear.

18
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:28,980
Thank you.

